      "title": "Collaborative Multi-Robot Search and Rescue: Planning, Coordination, Perception, and Active Vision",
      "takeaway": "This survey systematically reviews multi-robot systems for search and rescue (SAR), covering planning, coordination, perception, and active vision from both multi-agent perception and control perspectives. It is notable for addressing heterogeneous robots across different environments and highlighting open challenges such as shared autonomy, sim-to-real transfer, and active perception. For a researcher in legged robots and mobile manipulation, this survey provides a structured overview of coordination and perception methods that can be adapted to multi-robot legged systems, and it identifies gaps where learning-based approaches could be applied, such as sim-to-real transfer for locomotion in disaster scenarios.",
