      "title": "Mobile manipulation using NASA's Robonaut",
      "takeaway": "This paper describes an early mobile manipulation system combining a Robonaut upper body with a Segway RMP base, focusing on coordinated control of dexterous limbs on a mobile platform. It demonstrates human-robot interaction tasks such as object exchange and tool use, and discusses lessons learned for future designs. Although dated, it provides foundational insights into integrating mobility and manipulation, which is relevant to current mobile manipulation research. For a researcher in mobile manipulation, this historical perspective highlights challenges in balance, coordination, and human-robot interaction that remain relevant, and it can inform the design of new systems with modern control and learning methods.",
