      "title": "Interactive Model Predictive Control for Robot Navigation in Dense Crowds",
      "takeaway": "This paper presents an interactive model predictive control (MPC) framework for robot navigation in dense crowds, incorporating pedestrian intention and interaction prediction into the trajectory optimization. The multiobjective cost function balances real-time computation, collision avoidance, motion quality, and goal progress, and the approach is validated in simulations and real experiments, showing safe, efficient, and legible behaviors. For a researcher in optimal control and mobile manipulation, this work offers a method to handle dynamic environments with human presence, which is crucial for deploying mobile manipulators in populated spaces. The anticipative prediction model could be integrated with learning-based pedestrian models to further improve performance.",
